%description:
Tests rule (3) of the sender SWS avoidance (RFC 9293 section 3.8.6.2.1): a
segment smaller than the MSS goes out when it fills at least half of the
largest window that the peer offered. The server offers 700 bytes, less than
one MSS (1000), and the client sends 700-byte segments. A sender that held
each segment smaller than the MSS would send nothing (the defect that source
commit 69 repairs).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 2000"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1000
*.srv_tcp.advertisedWindow = 700

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:701(700) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 701 win 700 
[1.205 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 701:1401(700) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.407 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 1401 win 700 
[1.409 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1401:2001(600) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.611 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 2001 win 700 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
